s. Students will then apply the laws surrounding fiduciary duties and the business judgment rule to various simulated corporate transactions or decisions. Finally, students will assess how shareholder value is measured, including by looking at \"benefit corporations\" and how they differ from traditional corporations. Throughout the course, students will apply the course material to a series of hypothetical problems and proposed corporate actions. Accordingly, at the end of the course, students will have a toolkit", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: to MSLS students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "LA", "acadGroup": "LA", "lastTermsOffered": "2025SU, 2024SU, 2023FA, 2023SU", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2902, "crseId": 371213, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LEGAL", "catalogNbr": "5105", "titleShort": "Effective Communication Skills", "titleLong": "Effective Communication Skills", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1767, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/29/2025", "endDt": "08/15/2025", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "maf282", "firstName": "Michelle", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Fongyee Whelan"}], "pattern": "", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Enrollment limited to: Master of Science Legal Studies (MSLS) program students."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startD